**T-K1, THE COMMENT (on OXPD2-60, after T-C1 is verified or skipped):** THE COMMENT RULE: GET `issue/OXPD2-60/comment`: total 0 (as at drafting): go on; a comment whose inverse ADF text EQUALS the filled CM60 text: SKIP (write `{"kind": "skip-comment", "id": <id>}`); any other comment: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY jira OXPD2-60 holds comment <id>` (no POST). Then `POST /rest/api/3/issue/OXPD2-60/comment` with the body exactly `{"body": <ADF of the filled CM60 text>}` (no `visibility`, no `properties`, no other key): expect HTTP 201 and an `id`; write `{"kind": "comment", "t": "T-K1", "id": <id>, "clock": <date>}` at once; GET `issue/OXPD2-60/comment/<id>`: the inverse of its `body` EQUALS the filled CM60 text (control: a one-character mutant reads UNEQUAL). Write `{"kind": "verify-comment", ...}`.
