## HOLDS
**No sentence that anything is landed, fixed, approved, sent, shared, decided, created, commented, moved, ticked or done that a read of yours, a seat's record line or the product owner's frozen words do not show; no ruling put in anyone's mouth (the scope of the run's writes, the 2004/08 run, the call-back plan, the move of OXPD2-60 and every reading are the coordinator's).** No card id in any record line or Jira text; a person's name only inside his quoted words (PART 1) and in TEXT J-D (THE JIRA TEXT RULE). **The password's value is never read, printed or written by you; its document is never opened.** If a file replacement fails or reads back unequal: stop, find the cause, re-verify; never retry blindly.
**HOLD R, every file write:** build AND ENCODE the whole new content first, write it to a temp file BESIDE the target (same folder, suffix `.b2045.tmp`), then `os.replace` it onto the target; never open the live file for writing before the content exists; read the old file as BYTES and splice the new text into those bytes; the files may hold bytes above 126 (`CLAUDE.md` line 3 and `CLARIFICATIONS.md` line 1 do), so NEVER encode a whole file as ASCII: encode the ADDED text as UTF-8 and check those bytes; then compare every old line in order against the before-copy by the proof of its PART. Immediately before each `os.replace` read the target again: if its sha256 is not the one you built from, throw the build away and STOP (`STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <file> changed under the build`), except `history.md` (HOLD R2). A temp file left behind is quarantined, never deleted.
**HOLD R2, `history.md` only:** read the live bytes, build, and IMMEDIATELY before the `os.replace` read the file again: if its sha256 is not the one you built from, throw your build away and build again (at most three times, then `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY`), with P-5's check of line 3 each time. After the write read it back: your entry is there once, every line of the bytes you built from is there in order, line 1 unchanged. Say in STATUS how long the window between your last read and the replace was.
**HOLD J, every Jira request:** JSON requests through the project reader's `real_transport`, your fence in front, one process for all POSTs (its write log appended line by line and flushed); the log is the only source of the key and the id any record names; never print the `.env`, a token, an `Authorization` header or a request's credentials (bodies hold none).
**Shell:** no `cd`; one simple command per Bash call; absolute single-quoted paths (the project path holds a `!`); `python3 -I -B`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; no unquoted word that starts with an equals sign; never name a shell variable `path`. **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (Step 2); no message to any human but Jira's own notices of the create, the comment and the move; Jira writes only as PART 2 says; no Azure call; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a check you cannot explain is a STOP. **Git identity is never overridden** (this kit lets no seat commit: never `git -c user.name/user.email`, never `GIT_AUTHOR_*` / `GIT_COMMITTER_*`).

